				"⡇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				32,
				3
			],
			"Message": "docs(Mist): Overhaul architecture docs for WebSocket IPC pivot\n\nRebalance the documentation to reflect Mist's expanded role as both a local DNS server AND a direct WebSocket JSON-RPC transport for Sky↔Cocoon IPC. The previous docs centred on DNSSEC as the primary trust mechanism; the updated docs replace that with the shared-secret authenticated WebSocket path as the central transport for the ~95% of IPC traffic that is extension-API calls.\n\n- Add CC0 LICENSE file (Creative Commons CC0 1.0 Universal)\n- Rewrite Architecture.md goals and principles: drop DNSSEC as a core principle, replace with Authenticated Transport\n- Add detailed shared-secret auth flow to WebSocket section (X-Land-Secret header, ?secret= query param, Sec-WebSocket-Protocol entry, 403 rejection)\n- Update Mermaid diagrams to show both Cocoon and Sky as WebSocket peers, remove the Resolver→WebSocket arrow\n- Revise key components table to describe the JSON-RPC WebSocket role explicitly\n- Add the WebSocket dependency list (tokio-tungstenite, futures-util, hex, rand, Common)\n- Expand the connection paths table with separate rows for Cocoon↔Mist and Sky↔Mist WebSocket flows\n- Add License and Changelog sections to Architecture.md\n- Normalize emoji spacing throughout (HTML entity &#x2001; instead of literal emoji spaces)\n- Update README.md goals, table of principles, component table, integration section, and consumer matrix to reflect the dual DNS+WebSocket nature",
			"SHA": "534a6d2307986f68732989ff333fd4a8c4ae58a9"
		},
